WEBVTT

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.620
Both today and tomorrow, I've got time to kick back.

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.620
kyou mo ashita mo HIMAKKUSU

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:24.830
My family of four and I are going to stay the night.

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:24.830
gokazoku yonin de goippaku

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.670
Put on an Egyptian front and become a sphinx,

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.670
EGIPUTO kidori de SUFINKUSU

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.460
and for an American feeling, Texas!

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.460
AMERICA kibun de TEXAS

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.470
When you're sitting pretty, with enough and to spare,

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.470
yoyuu SHAKUSHAKUPPE itsumo

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.680
and yet you always shilly-shally,

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.680
funya funya de iruto

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:39.930
and your bitter face and bitter feelings both teeter-totter,

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:39.930
nigamushi hara no mushi nahe nahe to

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:43.390
it's time to get out of there!

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:43.390
tettai shichau yo

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:46.690
I am feeling Ultra Relax,

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:46.690
watashi ha URUTORA RIRAKKUSU

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.900
a wonderful, invincible Relax.

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.900
SUTEKI ni muteki na RIRAKKUSU

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:52.860
A one-step-above kind of Deluxe.

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:52.860
hito aji chigau ze DERAKKUSU

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:54.070
I may be a little jumbled,

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:54.070
toccharakatte mo

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:55.820
but when I'm called on, ba-ba-ba-ba-bang!

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:55.820
yobarerya PAPAPAPAAAN!

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.910
I always feel Relax,

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.910
watashi ha itsudemo RIRAKKUSU

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.910
a humble, simple, sort of Deluxe.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.910
WABISABI kikasete DERAKKUSU

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.830
Bright! Clear! Alert-headed, peep-peep!

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.830
BIKKARI! KIKKARI! saeteru ATAMA PII! PII!

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:07.960
Keep your eyes on me, okay?!

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:07.960
watashi no KOTO dake mitete ne!

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:36.200
I am Kurata Sana, Jinbo Junior High School first year student.

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:39.910
Manager Rei-kun, seems that he has too much time on his hands in New York.

00:01:39.910 --> 00:01:43.580
The one who looks like that guy in Japan, the American, Brad.

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:48.170
Broadway's Choreographer, Old Lady Michelle Hamilton.

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:53.130
Her husband, King Producer, Gary Hamilton... and actually he's Naozumi's father.

00:01:54.010 --> 00:01:56.130
This is their only child, Sicil Hamilton.

00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:00.720
The woman who suddenly appeared, Naozumi's mother Yuko-san.

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:04.220
The amazing bat Babbit.

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:06.560
New York Arc has 3 more episodes.

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:10.940
Having a really tough and bumpy time, Naozumi-kun.

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:15.900
Papa, This is All Your Fault!

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:17.320
Sorry for disturbing you!

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:20.700
A song sung by
a cheerful Sana-chan

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:27.410
Who cares what the adults are fighting over, what's the big deal?

00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:30.920
We're after all actors... together...

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:32.210
Dance... Babbit.

00:02:32.210 --> 00:02:37.010
Happily, dancing... we want to show our mambo dancing skills in New York.

00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:40.010
Singing... dancing... smiling...

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:43.640
If we fall...

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:47.230
Anyway, we want to make it big on Broadway.

00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:51.440
Oh Naozumi-kun, you seem to be very energetic today.

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:55.110
Ahh, I feel like I can heave a sigh of relief.

00:02:57.030 --> 00:03:01.110
I have a little more self respect for not returning to Japan.

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:02.820
That's good.

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:05.910
They're both strong,
Sana-chan and Naozumi-kun.

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:08.540
It's hard to believe that they're still kids.

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:12.330
Who said kids aren't strong anyway?

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:14.630
Ahh, that's true.

00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:19.340
But it's a happy thing that everyone's staying together.

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:20.260
What's that smell? Is it me?

00:03:19.340 --> 00:03:22.340
That's why today's breakfast shall have a Japanese touch...

00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:23.850
It's this!

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:25.810
Ah... it's the smell of Nato.

00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:30.440
Put it together... and it's called Smoked Nato Dried Fish with Rice!

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:35.060
This is not the taste of Japan!

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:35.110
Can this be eaten? Urgh.

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:39.530
Oh yes, Maeda-san... is not here today?

00:03:39.530 --> 00:03:43.660
Ah, that's because he had an accident at the airport.

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:46.410
What kind of accident is it?

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:46.410
Right, this is Maeda-san's latest report.

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:48.700
Oh! Wait for me, everyone!

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:55.040
Admitted to hospital again!

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:57.000
Welcome back!

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:57.460
I'm back again...

00:03:57.460 --> 00:03:59.050
Please take care...

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:01.760
Alright...

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:05.550
Sana-chan, are you sure you want to return to lessons so soon?

00:04:05.550 --> 00:04:07.850
What are you talking about, Unagi-san?

00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:09.060
You mean Usagi...

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:12.440
Once a decision is made, it should be done immediately.

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:15.060
Especially since I'm the one that all this is happening to now...

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:17.520
I have to learn from Sana-chan.

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:19.070
See ya, Rei-kun.

00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:23.110
Driver-san, please drive full force ahead!

00:04:23.110 --> 00:04:25.240
Hey Miss, are you from Japan?

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:27.700
Work hard!

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:31.200
I really admire you all you know...

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:31.540
This place you have to jump up and down...

00:04:31.540 --> 00:04:34.210
Bunto bunto jump jump

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:39.210
Komari komari komari komari komari

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:40.920
People who talk to themselves

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:40.960
Be quiet!

00:04:41.130 --> 00:04:43.130
First one here!

00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:51.520
Michelle-san...

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:54.020
Alright, I guess I'll stick to this dance step.

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:57.100
Ah...

00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:59.610
Good morning!

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:00.730
It's early.

00:05:00.730 --> 00:05:04.400
You always come this early?

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:06.910
Not really...

00:05:09.030 --> 00:05:11.910
I heard that you two came back from the airport.

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:12.830
Yes.

00:05:12.830 --> 00:05:16.750
I thought you two were just noisy and mischievous children...

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:19.290
I guess you two still have some drive...

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:24.010
Since you came back again, don't run away again.

00:05:24.010 --> 00:05:26.010
That is... of course...

00:05:26.510 --> 00:05:29.430
I'll be more stricter now so be prepared.

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:31.640
- Yes!
- Argh!

00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:35.730
Michelle-san has recognized our abilities somewhat now I guess...

00:05:35.730 --> 00:05:38.520
but tough means tough, huh?

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:39.900
Firstly...

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:41.020
Yes!

00:05:42.610 --> 00:05:45.610
What are you dragging on for? Use more strength!

00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:47.910
Yes!

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:50.910
Strengthen your legs!

00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:52.990
Yes!

00:05:52.990 --> 00:05:57.210
This is the punishment for escaping... she's definitely a strict old lady.

00:06:08.510 --> 00:06:10.720
Lift your hands higher,
follow the tempo!

00:06:26.940 --> 00:06:29.530
Toes must be stretched straight, follow the tempo!

00:06:45.250 --> 00:06:47.050
Nope, do it again.

00:06:50.180 --> 00:06:53.180
Ah, this is so tiring...

00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:58.310
For so many hours, I've danced until my limbs all feel so numb.

00:06:58.310 --> 00:06:59.850
Do you want to bathe?{check}

00:06:59.850 --> 00:07:02.650
I'm so hungry, let's hurry home.

00:07:02.650 --> 00:07:04.070
That's true.

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:08.030
Gary-san.

00:07:08.320 --> 00:07:13.910
I have some words that I would like to speak to Naozumi alone.

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:15.410
Wait a minute!

00:07:17.700 --> 00:07:19.540
What are you gonna do, Naozumi-kun?

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:23.420
If you don't want to,
it's ok to escape you know.

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:29.130
Although I don't know what he wants, it's still better to hear him out I guess.

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:31.050
Mou man tai...

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:37.140
Yeah, I've already thought things out between our relationship as a producer and an actor.

00:07:37.140 --> 00:07:38.980
I see, I understand.

00:07:41.230 --> 00:07:43.230
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:49.650
Naozumi-kun...

00:07:52.110 --> 00:07:56.280
Long time ago, hmm...
already 14 years I guess...

00:07:56.280 --> 00:08:01.620
When I was still young in Broadway I had some fame already

00:08:01.620 --> 00:08:06.540
and because of some joint project I went to Japan and met Yuko.

00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:14.930
I once loved Yuko... I treated it as love but Yuko didn't think of it that way.

00:08:14.930 --> 00:08:22.310
She loved the stage
and drama more than me.

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:26.520
A kind of passion that is burning and scary.

00:08:27.230 --> 00:08:29.570
I was defeated by that passion...

00:08:29.570 --> 00:08:34.610
No... to be truthful, I disliked that passion so I returned to America.

00:08:34.610 --> 00:08:40.080
However, I didn't know she already had my child.

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:45.960
After a while, she pursued me all the way to New York.

00:08:45.960 --> 00:08:51.050
She said she wanted to stand on stage again so I found some jobs for her,

00:08:51.050 --> 00:08:53.470
but they didn't really take off.

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:58.510
She couldn't succeed despite that passion which drove her to abandon me.

00:08:58.510 --> 00:09:01.350
This is a world which wants real talent.

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:07.440
After a few years, I heard that Yuko left behind a child in Japan and I was surprised.

00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:12.360
Immediately, I started investigations and that's how I found out about your existence.

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:17.070
You've done really well in the entertainment field.

00:09:17.070 --> 00:09:21.040
You are truly our... no... truly my child.

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:24.960
I held high expectations as I watched Water Palace.

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:29.540
I was the first one to watch it when it was finished.

00:09:30.290 --> 00:09:34.420
That was brilliant acting... I was moved.

00:09:34.420 --> 00:09:38.140
I was sure that you would succeed the same way on Broadway's stage.

00:09:38.140 --> 00:09:43.640
After that, I did not waste a single moment in calling you over.

00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:50.440
I wanted to keep all this under wraps until the musical was over

00:09:50.440 --> 00:09:54.570
because I wanted you to concentrate solely on stage...

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:59.320
but in the end it still affected you.

00:10:01.030 --> 00:10:04.040
It doesn't matter anymore.

00:10:06.370 --> 00:10:08.170
After this...

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:14.130
I hope that after the musical is over... you can still stay on in New York.

00:10:14.130 --> 00:10:15.130
Eh?

00:10:15.130 --> 00:10:19.590
I want to use my own hands to cultivate your budding talents.

00:10:19.590 --> 00:10:23.970
I have the power to give you a wonderful sparkling future

00:10:23.970 --> 00:10:26.520
and one day we can all live together.

00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:28.310
- Together?
- Yes.

00:10:29.940 --> 00:10:32.860
About this matter,
what does Michelle-san say?

00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:34.940
Eh? Michelle?

00:10:35.480 --> 00:10:38.820
Yeah, did Michelle-san agree to this?

00:10:38.820 --> 00:10:42.910
Well, err... I haven't talked to Michelle about this.

00:10:42.910 --> 00:10:44.830
What about Sicil?

00:10:44.830 --> 00:10:48.410
Well, I talked to Sicil a little about this.

00:10:48.410 --> 00:10:52.920
I've already made up my mind and Michelle and Sicil should understand as well.

00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:54.670
Yau man tai!

00:10:54.670 --> 00:11:00.010
That's rude, Gary-san. How can you say that with such confidence?

00:11:00.010 --> 00:11:01.300
Sana...

00:11:01.300 --> 00:11:02.510
Sana-chan...

00:11:02.510 --> 00:11:04.890
This week's Sana-chan who uses Cantonese.

00:11:04.890 --> 00:11:06.060
There's a problem.

00:11:04.930 --> 00:11:07.020
There's a problem

00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:16.980
{parte b}

00:11:17.150 --> 00:11:20.030
Babbit's Counting Song

00:11:19.860 --> 00:11:23.160
1  2,  1  2  3,  8

00:11:23.160 --> 00:11:25.830
Yelling out then breaking the ceramic tiles

00:11:25.830 --> 00:11:28.620
If you don't know karate then don't try it

00:11:28.620 --> 00:11:31.830
Yelling out then breaking the ceramic tiles

00:11:31.830 --> 00:11:34.630
If you don't know karate then don't try it

00:11:34.630 --> 00:11:37.630
1  2,  1  2  3,  9

00:11:37.630 --> 00:11:40.800
Crying, laughing and steaming, sticking your tongue out

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:43.720
I have a hundred faces, makes me so happy!

00:11:43.720 --> 00:11:46.930
Crying, laughing and steaming, sticking your tongue out

00:11:46.930 --> 00:11:49.810
I have a hundred faces, makes me so happy!

00:11:49.810 --> 00:11:52.810
1  2,  1  2  3,  10

00:11:52.810 --> 00:11:55.610
Tendon, udon, oyakodon

00:11:55.610 --> 00:11:58.610
Babbit likes maccha-don

00:11:58.610 --> 00:12:01.610
Tendon, udon, oyakodon

00:12:01.610 --> 00:12:04.820
Babbit likes maccha-don

00:12:04.820 --> 00:12:07.990
I'll see you next in the Japan chapters!

00:12:08.330 --> 00:12:13.080
Sana, why are you here?
You seem very angry, why?

00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:17.380
Hey Mr. Gary, you don't understand?

00:12:17.380 --> 00:12:18.590
What is it?

00:12:18.590 --> 00:12:23.800
Ahh... this is terrible... the whole Hamilton family is like America's oyakodon-baka.

00:12:24.930 --> 00:12:27.100
Where... Oyakodon?

00:12:27.100 --> 00:12:30.640
Stupid... you need to put stupid behind the oyakodon...

00:12:30.640 --> 00:12:34.020
but putting it on has no meaning anyway.

00:12:34.690 --> 00:12:40.070
I'll put it this way, Gary-san. Haven't you realized that Sicil might be scared?

00:12:40.070 --> 00:12:41.320
Scared?

00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:45.410
Right, thinking that she might become a child who nobody wants.

00:12:45.410 --> 00:12:46.950
A child who nobody wants?

00:12:46.950 --> 00:12:50.160
Ahhh... you don't know anything! You slow-witted man!

00:12:50.160 --> 00:12:52.870
Hey Mr. Gary Hamilton-san...

00:12:52.870 --> 00:12:58.040
In a family, when there's suddenly another person, it causes a very big and serious problem.

00:12:58.040 --> 00:13:00.460
You actually think you can settle everything by yourself!

00:13:00.460 --> 00:13:04.550
Hey Mr. Gary! You've always decided on matters by yourself... right?

00:13:04.550 --> 00:13:06.010
No... I...

00:13:06.010 --> 00:13:09.720
Attention! Bow! Sit down!

00:13:09.720 --> 00:13:11.930
Naozumi-kun, come here a minute!

00:13:14.310 --> 00:13:15.640
Action!

00:13:17.230 --> 00:13:22.030
Ahh... don't be shy, speak up. This is what the Hamilton family lacks I suppose.

00:13:22.030 --> 00:13:26.570
We'll be over there so please discuss this slowly.

00:13:26.780 --> 00:13:28.530
The Hamilton Family Meeting

00:13:47.430 --> 00:13:49.220
Say it!

00:13:50.640 --> 00:13:52.680
- This is Do.
- Do Re Mi's Do?

00:13:52.680 --> 00:13:55.430
Right, and this is Re.

00:14:05.530 --> 00:14:06.900
Say it already!

00:14:06.490 --> 00:14:08.700
If this was a video tape
we could at least fast forward

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:08.490
I'm sleeping...

00:14:11.330 --> 00:14:13.410
Err...

00:14:13.410 --> 00:14:14.330
What is it?

00:14:14.330 --> 00:14:16.750
No... Nothing...

00:14:23.920 --> 00:14:26.800
Well... err... today's weather is good.

00:14:26.800 --> 00:14:28.680
Eh? Yeah...

00:14:42.730 --> 00:14:45.780
Do you know that's a marching line?

00:14:46.400 --> 00:14:48.990
Ahh... ants...

00:14:52.030 --> 00:14:55.580
I've always been wanting to ask you...

00:14:55.580 --> 00:14:57.540
What is it?

00:14:57.540 --> 00:14:59.830
What's the difference between a trumpet and a lapa?

00:14:59.830 --> 00:15:05.550
Well... err... eh? Lapa?

00:14:59.830 --> 00:15:05.550
Chinese call trumpets "Lapa".

00:15:05.840 --> 00:15:10.720
Wait a minute... let me check what the difference is. You can continue, you know...

00:15:13.510 --> 00:15:16.890
Just now Sana...

00:15:16.890 --> 00:15:22.310
Sana mentioned that Sicil...

00:15:22.860 --> 00:15:27.440
She mentioned that Sicil might be afraid...

00:15:27.440 --> 00:15:30.280
She might become a child who nobody wants.

00:15:30.280 --> 00:15:32.910
Nobody wants? Sicil?

00:15:40.620 --> 00:15:41.620
Sicil?

00:15:41.620 --> 00:15:49.170
Lapa... lapa looks like something which looks like lapa... lapa looks like this...

00:15:49.170 --> 00:15:54.140
Looks like this? Hmm...
What language calls it lapa?

00:15:54.390 --> 00:15:56.390
Another new and difficult question

00:16:00.100 --> 00:16:01.940
Sicil.

00:16:01.940 --> 00:16:03.560
Sicil.

00:16:04.860 --> 00:16:07.480
Because I can't dance.

00:16:08.820 --> 00:16:10.900
Don't tell me...

00:16:11.240 --> 00:16:15.570
I do not want a child which can't dance... that's not my child!

00:16:16.330 --> 00:16:20.790
You heard it... you heard it, didn't you?

00:16:23.620 --> 00:16:30.920
I do not know why I said that myself... it was so chaotic back then.

00:16:30.920 --> 00:16:35.260
Sicil, it could be too late to say this now,

00:16:35.260 --> 00:16:39.100
but Mama has always been blaming herself for that matter...

00:16:39.100 --> 00:16:43.230
Papa too! Papa did not
want me either anymore.

00:16:43.230 --> 00:16:45.100
What are you talking about, Sicil?

00:16:45.100 --> 00:16:50.110
In the past you used to always bring me to watch musicals but after that incident...

00:16:50.110 --> 00:16:55.950
I was afraid that you would feel sad and uncomfortable seeing other people dance.

00:16:55.950 --> 00:16:58.160
Why were you deciding for me?

00:16:58.160 --> 00:17:03.160
I've always loved to see musicals and wanted to watch them with Papa.

00:17:03.160 --> 00:17:05.540
But I've always been by myself...

00:17:05.540 --> 00:17:09.420
Sicil, I was looking out
for your best interests.

00:17:09.420 --> 00:17:12.670
No, I have indeed become a child who nobody wants.

00:17:12.670 --> 00:17:15.880
Papa and Mama no longer want a child who cannot dance.

00:17:15.880 --> 00:17:17.840
That's not true.

00:17:17.840 --> 00:17:19.430
That's right, Sicil.

00:17:24.020 --> 00:17:29.230
Regardless of whether you can dance or not, Sicil is still Sicil.

00:17:29.230 --> 00:17:31.820
That's right, Sicil.

00:17:31.820 --> 00:17:35.780
You are our most precious daughter.

00:17:42.790 --> 00:17:44.660
Hey, about Lapa...

00:17:46.370 --> 00:17:48.170
I think Lapa is Latin.

00:17:48.460 --> 00:17:50.420
Still talking about it?

00:17:48.750 --> 00:17:50.710
Is that true?

00:17:50.710 --> 00:17:57.430
Don't be so serious about it.
Blow me some tunes.

00:18:18.990 --> 00:18:20.820
Hi!

00:18:20.820 --> 00:18:22.120
Hello.

00:18:22.120 --> 00:18:28.330
To think... having such a talk is a good thing.

00:18:28.920 --> 00:18:33.550
To wrap things up...

00:18:33.550 --> 00:18:36.090
everything was my fault.

00:18:38.010 --> 00:18:43.930
I'm already feeling hungry so we'll wait till Part 2 before continuing.

00:18:43.930 --> 00:18:45.970
That's really good!

00:18:45.970 --> 00:18:49.850
So see you again... we'll leave other things for next time.

00:18:49.850 --> 00:18:52.730
We'll go home now then.

00:18:52.730 --> 00:18:55.730
That's a good idea.

00:18:55.730 --> 00:18:57.070
Right.

00:19:06.410 --> 00:19:12.830
Yup yup, the American oyakodon-baka has grown up a little now.

00:19:23.220 --> 00:19:25.260
Can I come out now?

00:19:27.020 --> 00:19:28.850
What are you doing, Brad?

00:19:28.850 --> 00:19:32.310
I've been here all along but there wasn't a good time for me to come out.

00:19:32.310 --> 00:19:34.310
All along? Starting from when...?

00:19:34.310 --> 00:19:37.610
The difference between trumpet and lapa...

00:19:37.610 --> 00:19:40.320
Are you an idiot?

00:19:40.320 --> 00:19:44.530
Brad has to reveal his true feelings as well... to the other party.

00:19:44.530 --> 00:19:46.030
What are you talking about?

00:19:46.030 --> 00:19:49.200
Something to tell Sicil?

00:19:49.620 --> 00:19:52.000
What? Tell what?

00:19:52.000 --> 00:19:54.540
Sana-chan is still as slow as ever...

00:19:54.540 --> 00:19:55.670
Can I come out now?

00:19:56.500 --> 00:20:00.970
Don't joke!
What's wrong with my acting?

00:20:00.970 --> 00:20:03.590
You're the one who can't act!

00:20:03.590 --> 00:20:08.060
What? Who do you think you are?
You're even worse than those musical people.

00:20:08.060 --> 00:20:10.230
- What did you say?
- Calm down.

00:20:10.230 --> 00:20:14.020
Shut up! You're also another lousy scriptwriter.

00:20:14.020 --> 00:20:18.020
What? You too! You can't even memorize your lines properly.

00:20:18.020 --> 00:20:19.530
I quit.

00:20:19.530 --> 00:20:21.320
I quit too.

00:20:21.320 --> 00:20:25.200
What the...? I was going to tell you two to scram anyway!

00:20:25.200 --> 00:20:27.030
I quit...

00:20:27.030 --> 00:20:33.120
Wait a minute... what's wrong with everybody? Wait...

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:37.460
Do what you like!

00:20:37.460 --> 00:20:42.510
There are other replacements which I can easily find. There are a lot!

00:20:43.430 --> 00:20:48.010
Mama, Shimura-san, Onda-san, Maro-chan, are you fine?

00:20:48.010 --> 00:20:50.020
We're all fine over here.

00:20:50.020 --> 00:20:52.230
A nostalgic Japan.

00:20:52.230 --> 00:20:57.150
The official performance is coming closer and everyday, preparations are mounting.

00:20:57.150 --> 00:21:02.400
I can't wait! I want to jump up and dance the mambo!

00:21:02.400 --> 00:21:07.280
Mama, do come over soon.
I'll be waiting. Sana.

00:21:09.030 --> 00:21:11.540
Back to New York

00:21:09.200 --> 00:21:11.910
New York, I'm back again.

00:21:11.910 --> 00:21:13.330
Ahhh?

00:21:13.330 --> 00:21:17.000
What, Rei-kun? What happened?

00:21:17.000 --> 00:21:18.750
This... this...

00:21:19.170 --> 00:21:20.340
Look!

00:21:20.340 --> 00:21:25.430
Yuko Mizukuchi's performance of "Over The River" has stopped operations.

00:21:25.430 --> 00:21:30.310
She had her just desserts!

00:21:30.310 --> 00:21:33.430
Stopped operations...

00:21:33.430 --> 00:21:35.100
Naozumi-kun...

00:21:35.100 --> 00:21:39.610
Don't worry about me, it has nothing to do with me now. No worries.

00:21:39.610 --> 00:21:40.820
I see...

00:21:40.820 --> 00:21:42.820
The tea is ready.

00:21:42.820 --> 00:21:44.400
Thank you.

00:21:45.110 --> 00:21:48.490
Ah, isn't today the day you're supposed to call back to Japan?

00:21:48.490 --> 00:21:51.330
Oh yeah, I forgot. Hope Mama's fine.

00:21:51.330 --> 00:21:53.540
I wonder whether Mama is fine.

00:21:53.540 --> 00:21:55.910
That person is definitely fine.

00:21:55.910 --> 00:21:59.840
It's coming soon, isn't it? Sana's mother and others are coming to watch the musical.

00:21:59.840 --> 00:22:00.710
Yup.

00:22:00.710 --> 00:22:03.000
I can't wait to meet them.

00:22:04.630 --> 00:22:06.630
Coming!

00:22:06.630 --> 00:22:07.800
Rick-san!

00:22:11.140 --> 00:22:13.770
Please help, Naozumi.

00:22:16.480 --> 00:22:20.940
I know I don't have the right to beg you

00:22:20.940 --> 00:22:27.200
but Yuko is down and out and I can't help her by myself.

00:22:29.610 --> 00:22:31.490
I beg of you, Naozumi!

00:22:33.620 --> 00:22:35.200
I beg of you!

00:22:36.250 --> 00:22:40.130
matte  mou wakaretai no yo

00:22:36.250 --> 00:22:40.130
"Wait... I want us to split up", I said

00:22:40.830 --> 00:22:45.510
ima  KISU wo sorashinagara itta

00:22:40.830 --> 00:22:45.510
Just now, when I turned away from your kiss

00:22:46.720 --> 00:22:50.970
Gutto  tsukihanasu kono me ni

00:22:46.720 --> 00:22:50.970
Under the gaze of my sharp, firm eyes

00:22:51.300 --> 00:22:56.390
odoroite  anata wa damatta ne

00:22:51.300 --> 00:22:56.390
You were startled, and didn't say a word

00:22:56.890 --> 00:23:01.350
tooranakya ikenai michi wo

00:22:56.890 --> 00:23:01.350
You can't see what's in front of you

00:23:02.060 --> 00:23:06.610
saketecha  saki wa mienai janai

00:23:02.060 --> 00:23:06.610
If you walk off the road you have to go along

00:23:07.360 --> 00:23:11.870
GURUGURU to tada  mayoikomu yori mo

00:23:07.360 --> 00:23:11.870
Let's gather some courage and set this straight now

00:23:12.490 --> 00:23:18.080
hakkiri to ima  yuuki wo dasou yo

00:23:12.490 --> 00:23:18.080
Rather than walking around in circles

00:23:20.290 --> 00:23:24.790
Love Me Deeper  daite  kizutsuketai

00:23:20.290 --> 00:23:24.790
Love me deeper, hold me, I wanna hurt you

00:23:25.550 --> 00:23:30.050
Touch Me, PINCH ni oitsumete ageru

00:23:25.550 --> 00:23:30.050
ouch me, I'll pin you down with this pinch

00:23:30.720 --> 00:23:35.010
Deeper Deeper  hayaku  honki ni natte

00:23:30.720 --> 00:23:35.010
Deeper, deeper, quick  get real

00:23:35.930 --> 00:23:41.140
anata to naite mitai kara

00:23:35.930 --> 00:23:41.140
Because I wanna try crying with you

00:23:41.230 --> 00:23:45.610
Love Me Deeper  daite  umarekawatte

00:23:41.230 --> 00:23:45.610
Love me deeper, hold me, be reborn

00:23:46.360 --> 00:23:50.950
Hold Me, PINCH wo kirinukete hoshii

00:23:46.360 --> 00:23:50.950
Take me, I want you to get through this pinch

00:23:51.570 --> 00:23:56.030
Deeper Deeper  hayaku  me wo samashite

00:23:51.570 --> 00:23:56.030
Deeper, deeper, quick  open your eyes

00:23:56.740 --> 00:24:03.120
watashi hitori wo  sou aishite

00:23:56.740 --> 00:24:03.120
And make me  the only one you love

00:24:06.380 --> 00:24:10.380
Hi. What will happen in the next Child's Toy?

00:24:10.380 --> 00:24:16.680
The selfish Yuko-mama, facing the stoppage of her show. Makes me want to cheer.

00:24:16.680 --> 00:24:18.470
But how is Naozumi feeling?

00:24:18.470 --> 00:24:21.600
And now our premiere is coming up.

00:24:21.600 --> 00:24:23.600
I think I had a bad dream.

00:24:23.600 --> 00:24:26.270
Naozumi, will it be a smooth ride onto the stage?

00:24:26.270 --> 00:24:30.900
Next episode of Child's Toy, number 78:The clash between Naozumi and Yuko.

00:24:30.900 --> 00:24:32.990
The first and the last father and son war,

00:24:32.990 --> 00:24:35.780
There are so many mountains to climb and roads to cross!
